    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0104" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg24"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lord to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Buenos Ayres</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-16"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 192.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to confirm the
                    Department’s cablegram<anchor n="b" xml:id="d15-f1"/> of May 24th last, and to
                    report that, in compliance therewith, I immediately communicated to the minister
                    for foreign relations the request there in contained, and that the Argentine
                    Government at once granted the desired permission.</p>
                <p>I have the further honor to inform you that I have suitably acknowledged the
                    courtesy of the Argentine Government and have instructed the United States
                    consuls within its territory to use their good offices in behalf of the
                    Government and citizens of Cuba until further notice.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. P. Lord.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
